## 1. Letter from the CEO

To our shareholders, employees, partners, and customers,

2024 was a landmark year for MedSync Health, marked by significant growth, strategic expansion, and the successful closing of our Series D funding round. We solidified our position as a leader in the healthcare technology sector, driven by our mission to seamlessly integrate healthcare systems and improve patient outcomes.

Our total revenue reached **AED 485.10 million**, representing a 32.0% year-over-year growth from AED 367.50 million in FY 2023. This growth was fueled by the continued success of our core products and the strategic expansion of our footprint in the EMEA and APAC regions.

While we continue to invest heavily in innovation, resulting in an operating loss of **AED 19.72 million** and a net loss of **AED 22.49 million**, these investments are critical for maintaining our competitive edge and preparing for long-term value creation. Our successful Series D round, which raised **AED 551.25 million**, has provided us with a strong cash position of **AED 441.00 million**, giving us a runway of approximately 23.5 months to achieve profitability and execute our planned IPO.

We remain committed to our 1,200 dedicated employees across our global offices and look forward to another year of transformative growth.

*Dr. Sarah Chen*  
*Chief Executive Officer, MedSync Health*

